      "answer_markdown": "Your gas bill went up by {F1}, rising from {F2} in December to {F3} in January [E1][E5]. The January period was colder, which added {F4} to the bill [E1][E2]. The later bill also covered more days than the December one, adding {F5} [E1][E2]. The unit rate went down, which took {F7} off the bill [E1][E2][E4]. The standing charge went up, adding {F8} [E1][E2][E4]. The earlier bill had been based on an estimate that was too low, so it was corrected and {F6} was removed from the January bill [E1][E2][E3]. Other possible causes such as credit changes, a fuel switch or a change in use beyond the weather were checked and ruled out.",
